# Project instructions

## Start here

- Read `.ai/WORKFLOW.md` for the main-agent workflow and completion contract.
- Read `docs/ai/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` when present before changing product behavior.
- Read `docs/ai/ARCHITECTURE.md` when present before changing boundaries or data flow.
- Use only commands documented in `docs/ai/COMMANDS.md` or discovered from the repository.
- Record material technical decisions in existing project documentation; avoid creating empty documents.

## Working contract

- Preserve existing behavior unless the task explicitly changes it.
- Keep secrets, generated output, runtime data, and personal data out of Git.
- Inspect the working tree before editing and preserve unrelated changes.
- Run the smallest relevant verification first, then broader checks when risk justifies them.
- Never deploy, publish, submit, send messages, or perform destructive data operations without explicit authorization.

## Agent workflow

- The selected tool's main conversation is the lead. In OpenCode select `lead`.
- Discuss a bounded plan with the user and wait for approval before implementing it. Existing explicit approval remains valid; do not ask again for the same plan.
- After approval, continue through implementation, verification, and at most two repair rounds until the criteria pass or a specific blocker remains.
- Only the lead delegates. Specialists return evidence to the lead and do not delegate further.
- Use explorer and planner roles for bounded read-only discovery and design when useful. A small change does not require every role.
- Use the implementer for one clearly bounded write scope.
- Use reviewer, tester, and security roles as independent checks.
- Do not let multiple agents edit overlapping files concurrently.
- Use `.ai/HANDOFF.md` for unfinished cross-session or cross-model work.
- Never silently switch from a local model to a cloud model, or invoke a different AI client as a worker.
- Keep technical instructions and agent artifacts in English. Speak Swedish with the user unless they request another language.
<!-- ai-kit:end -->
